<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Despenser family</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Despensers</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Despensers were an English noble family. Hugh Despenser the Younger, a favourite of Edward II, gained the lordship of Glamorgan through his marriage to Eleanor de Clare, a co-heiress of the Clare earls of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gloucester">Gloucester</a>, and he and his father dominated the government until both were executed in 1326. The family kept Glamorgan until the early 15th century, when it passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beauchamp-family">Beauchamps</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/despenser-family.jpg" alt="Despenser family" width="320" height="262" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coronet_of_a_British_Baron.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
